 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 676998,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You go to a new hairstylist, and he suggests that you add highlights to your hair, cut off a few inches, and add some layers. You’re hesitant to do so because you can’t imagine what you’re going to look like with your new hairstyle. What characteristic of service does this example illustrate?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1345244,
     "content_html": "Service intangibility",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "Service intangibility refers to the fact that you can&#8217;t see or touch a service before it is performed."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345243,
     "content_html": "Service variability",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Service variability may be defined as the changes in the quality of the same service provided by different service providers."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345242,
     "content_html": "Service perishability",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. The concept of service perishability states that services cannot be stored in inventory for future use or sale."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345241,
     "content_html": "Service inseparability",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Service inseparability means that the production and consumption of a service cannot be separated from the provider of that service."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
